{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":304,"recorded_at":1780531400000603,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"call_id":"call_01a0b35ea64273c6932c6b492e614a75","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1geqhj/TASK-260830-1geqhj_results-rev4.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj rev4 — producer results\n2|\n3|Task: implement `ax pane` SESSION_ID enforcement wrapper\n4|(rev4 rework of review-verdict-rev3: 1 P1 class at two sites with\n5|one root cause, 1 P2, 8 P3). Trunk: `2fc6d50`\n6|(`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, headings byte-identical to\n7|v0.6.0 in scope); `origin/main` verified equal to the candidate\n8|base before handoff, so no refresh was needed. Candidate left\n9|UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot. No\n10|partial-attempt recovery was needed: the worktree held the rev3\n11|candidate UNCOMMITTED (`M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n12|`?? internal/axpane/`) with no commit past the checkpoint.\n13|\n14|## Finding-by-finding table\n15|\n16|| Finding | Change (production call site) | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n17|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n18|| P1-1 agreement parks the post-takeover lifecycle | Deleted `leaseCheckpointAgrees` from `checkMaterialization` and `admitCheckpoint` (`decide.go`); added the one implication arm directly after the fencing arm in `Decide`: checkpoint-carrying winner + null fold parks `restore_policy` (`errSuccessorNullFold`) | `TestDecidePostTakeoverDivergedBaseLaunches`, `TestRunPostTakeoverRestoreLaunchesWithNewestClosure` (launch under the fix; parked before it), `TestDecideSuccessorNullFoldParks`, `TestRunSuccessorNullFoldParks`, `TestRunPostTakeoverStaleBaseParks` | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-successor-nullfold.log` |\n19|| P1-1 profile closure from the handoff base | `Run` loads the closure from the checkpoint actually resumed — required checkpoint, else the fold's newest via `LoadCheckpoint`, else the session head — never `Winner.Checkpoint` (`run.go`); the unknown-store guard now keys on the published newest | `TestRunPostTakeoverLaunchCarriesNewestClosureStandardToYolo`, `TestRunPostTakeoverLaunchCarriesNewestClosureYoloToStandard` (both directions through `Run`), `TestRunNoCkptStorePublishedNewestFails`, `TestRunNewestAbsentFromStoreFails` | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-closure-source.log` (mutant re-reads `Winner.Checkpoint`, launches stale yolo, dies) |\n20|| P2-1 post-window same-pair race reports launch | `Store.Supersede`/`installPair` report the replay (`binding.go`, `(Binding, bool, error)`); `Run` flips the replayed post-window outcome to `ActionReattach` with the recorded receipt (`run.go`) | `TestRunPostWindowSamePairRaceReattaches` (hook-played race through `Run`); store-level `TestSupersedeConcurrentSamePairReplays` asserts the signal | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-supersede-replay.log` |\n21|| P3-1 window closes on the lease checkpoint | No production change (the predicate already reads the fold only); added the negative and the harness row | `TestRunWindowLeaseCheckpointNullFoldRefuses` | `mutants/pass1/N-window-lease-checkpoint.log` |\n22|| P3-2 `Run` swallows the fold error | No production change (the error already propagates); added the negative and the harness row | `TestRunUnfoldableChainFails` | `mutants/pass1/N-run-fold-error.log` |\n23|| P3-3 ratio 39/43 | Re-derived on the fixed tree (see below) | — (measurement, not a gate) | `ratio-check.log` |\n24|| P3-4 fabricated 27-command list | This document reports the configured `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` verbatim with real exits (see below) | — | `cmd/cmd01-*.log` … `cmd/cmd27-*.log` |\n25|| P3-5 phantom matrix names | rev4 matrix names only tests verified present via `go test -list` | — | `ratio-check.log` |\n26|| P3-6 `realmRowUsable` restates reconcile | Stated as a bound (code comment + TRACEABILITY): the aggregate `Reconcile` error carries no per-object identity and liveness shares the generic mismatch code, so no per-row verdict can be derived; classification-only, fail-closed both directions | `TestDecideExpiredRealmRowRefusesUnavailable`, `TestDecidePreRebootRealmRowRefusesUnavailable`, `TestDecideLiveRealmRowBackendFaultStands` (unchanged) | `axpane-test-v.log` |\n27|| P3-7 identity not bound to SESSION_ID | `checkProviderIdentity` binds the validated record's own `session_id` (`checkIdentitySession`, `decide.go`); foreign record refuses `invalid_config` | `TestDecideIdentityForeignSessionRefuses` | `axpane-test-v.log`; `mutants/pass1/N-identity-session.log` |\n28|| P3-8 false prose | README profile sentence, TRACEABILITY rows, and the rev3 LOGBOOK entry (explicit REVERSAL paragraph, following the rev2 precedent) corrected | — | candidate diff |\n29|\n30|Stated bound added with P1-1: binding the handoff base to a\n31|checkpoint the chain published is the takeover leaf's obligation —\n32|this leaf compares the base against nothing (TRACEABILITY.md,\n33|`Decide` comment).\n34|\n35|## AC coverage: 43 of 43 rows driven\n36|\n37|Measured, not restated: 43 data rows counted in\n38|`internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`, every named test verified\n39|present via `go test -list`, zero rows without a named test, and\n40|the full package suite green (`ratio-check.log`,\n41|`axpane-test-v.log`: 192 `--- PASS`, 0 `--- FAIL`). The four rows\n42|the rev3 reviewer measured unfaithful now pin the post-takeover\n43|launch positives: materialization and checkpoint rows drive the\n44|C1-sourced launch and the stale-base park, the after-restore row\n45|drives both owners, and the profile row drives both directions\n46|plus the restore closure through `Run`.\n47|\n48|## Negative and mutant evidence\n49|\n50|- 11 new committed tests in `internal/axpane/rev4_test.go`, 3\n51|  rewritten in `rev3_test.go` (agreement negatives became the\n52|  diverged-base positive and the null-fold negative; the no-store\n53|  guard test follows the newest), plus replay-signal assertions\n54|  on the `Supersede` tests.\n55|- `mutant_harness.py`: 53/53 rows match on two full passes — 52\n56|  KILLED + the SURVIVED control. New rows: `N-successor-nullfold`\n57|  (null-fold conditional), `N-closure-source` (re-reads\n58|  `Winner.Checkpoint`), `N-supersede-replay` (replay keeps\n59|  launch), `N-window-lease-checkpoint`, `N-run-fold-error`,\n60|  `N-identity-session`, `N-run-newest-absent`; re-anchored:\n61|  `N-run-ckpt-store`, `N-supersede-no-replace`; deleted with the\n62|  equality: `N-materialization-agreement`, `N-checkpoint-agreement`.\n63|  Per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in `mutants/pass1/`\n64|  (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); production\n65|  blobs verified byte-identical before/after (`blob-oids-*.txt`).\n66|- Crash/idempotency: unchanged no-replace link commits on both\n67|  install paths, hook-armed seams, real-SIGKILL test; the replay\n68|  signal adds no new durable write.\n69|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate\n70|  inspects source text.\n71|\n72|## Validation suite (configured commands, in order)\n73|\n74|Every command below is quoted verbatim from\n75|`task-board.config.json`\n76|`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (27 commands) and\n77|was executed once against the exact candidate tree; logs in `cmd/`.\n78|\n79|| # | Command | Exit |\n80|| --- | --- | --- |\n81|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\"` | 0 |\n82|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n83|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n84|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 (38 packages ok, 21766 `--- PASS`, 0 package `FAIL`) |\n85|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | 0 (38 ok, 0 data races; axpane 17.5s) |\n86|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 (axpane 80.9%) |\n87|| 7–12 | rpcwire/scalar/canonicaljson fuzz ×6 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×6 |\n88|| 13–20 | secconftest fuzz ×8 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×8 |\n89|| 21 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (registry untouched: contracts=64, sections=36, clauses 49/569) |\n90|| 22 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0 |\n91|| 23 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n92|| 24 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n93|| 25 | JSON validation over tracked `*.json` | 0 |\n94|| 26 | `task-board validate` | 0 (185 pre-existing board-hygiene notes on other elements, unrelated to this candidate) |\n95|| 27 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n96|\n97|Note on cmd4: the log contains indented `--- FAIL` lines that are\n98|nested expected-failure output inside passing tests (e.g. the\n99|resumesmoke negative demonstrations); every package reports `ok`\n100|and the command exits 0.\n101|\n102|## Files changed\n103|\n104|- `internal/axpane/` (new package, still untracked):\n105|  `decide.go` (null-fold arm, agreement deleted, identity session\n106|  bind), `run.go` (closure source, newest-based guard,\n107|  replay flip), `binding.go` (replay signal), `errors.go`\n108|  (null-fold + identity causes), `doc.go`, `rev4_test.go` (new),\n109|  `rev3_test.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `mutant_harness.py`,\n110|  `TRACEABILITY.md` (rewrites above).\n111|- `README.md`: package section (additive: implication, closure\n112|  source, identity bind, 52-mutant count).\n113|- `LOGBOOK.md`: rev4 entry + explicit rev3 REVERSAL (additive).\n114|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n115|\n116|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n117|\n118|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added;\n119|mesh refresh is the caller-reported `Verified` fact; the\n120|dead-realm mapping fires only when the caller needs the realm\n121|row, submitted a realm row, and none is usable; the handoff-base\n122|binding is the takeover leaf's obligation; the realm usability\n123|predicate copy is classification-only. `internal/traceability`\n124|untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n125|\n126|## Handoff\n127|\n128|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n129|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n130|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_results-rev4.md`,\n131|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix-rev4.md`,\n132|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_rev4-evidence.tar.gz`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":305,"recorded_at":1780531400000605,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"call_id":"call_01a0b35ea7e57102b600c2b26e902ddf","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-kkh1an/TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-kkh1an — producer results (rev4 rework)\n2|\n3|Rework of CR revision 3 after RUN-260918-f6b44c (claude-opus-5 max):\n4|CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1 — one P2 production finding (F3), one\n5|P2 evidence finding (E3), five P3. Everything else from rev3 stands:\n6|the reviewer confirmed F1/F2/E1/E2 closed with their own instruments\n7|(including real SIGKILLs at two seams), the shipped harness 100/100\n8|twice, the 84-of-84 ratio re-derived, the full suite green, and\n9|hygiene clean. This run keeps all of it and closes every finding\n10|below. Trunk base `c3aae73` (unchanged since rev3; no refresh needed —\n11|`origin/main` still `c3aae73` at handoff), SPEC\n12|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, same heading numbers (§13.7 added\n13|to the cited scope for the cold force-takeover rule). The v0.7.0\n14|adoption figures are unchanged. `internal/traceability` untouched per\n15|the Story contract (final leaf TASK-260830-2056mm carries the\n16|registry bindings and the re-pin); `internal/fencing` gained the\n17|reviewer-sanctioned exported verdict plus its tests and one doc\n18|sentence, nothing else. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree\n19|for handoff snapshot.\n20|\n21|Inherited state: this run started from the rev3 candidate tree in the\n22|Story worktree (`M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n23|`M internal/axpane/decide.go`, `M internal/terminalbackend/…` ×4,\n24|`?? internal/terminstance/` — the reviewer-confirmed rev3 delta).\n25|All rev3 production code, tests, and harness rows were kept except\n26|the two rows reworked below; the changes are the only delta.\n27|\n28|## Finding-by-finding table\n29|\n30|| Finding | Change (production call site) | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n31|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n32|| F3: grant-less stale members never fenced (`repeat-of: rev2 F2`) | New landed `fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner` (`internal/fencing/staleness.go`): the direction/tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner without the grant precondition; `ObserveFencing` (`fencing.go`) consults it on every non-park outcome and fences on decided-stale from a live source. No local tuple comparison; the relative question needs no fallback | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessStaleFences` (48 transitions; fails pre-fix: 48 no-transition — verified by reverting the composition: 49 `--- FAIL` lines) | `terminstance-test-v.log`, `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-fencing-verdict-*.log`, `N-fencing-verdict-composition.log` (12 rows) |\n33|| E3: per-effect recheck pinned on the tuple axis only (`repeat-of: rev2 E2`) | No production change (the loop re-reads `Now()` per effect); committed witness + narrowing row. Both E1 expired members re-keyed onto the late-deadline instant so they kill on the receipt | `TestRV3W_M1_AuthExpiryRecheckedBeforeEachEffect` (fails under the entry-instant mutant: everything commits, `error = nil`) | `terminstance-test-v.log`, `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-recheck-auth-expiry.log` |\n34|| P3-1: evidence bound edge unwitnessed | No production change (shared `checkSortedUniqueEvidenceWhere`); committed witness + narrowing row | `TestRV3W_M2_EvidenceBoundEdge` (fails under the 257 mutant on both surfaces) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-result-evidence-bound.log` |\n35|| P3-2: conditional disposition unpinned at engine | No production change (`DispositionFor` mapping existed); committed witness + narrowing row | `TestRV3W_M3_ConditionalCapabilityDisposition` (fails under the collapsed mutant: `status_first` ≠ `required_operator_action`) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-conditional-disposition.log` |\n36|| P3-3: last_operation_id grammar unwitnessed | No production change (the arm existed); committed witness + narrowing row | `TestRV3W_M8_StatusLastOperationGrammar` (fails under the empty-admitting mutant) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-status-last-operation-empty.log` |\n37|| P3-4: proof-kind sibling admitted under narrowing | No production change (single `ParseProviderProofKind` arm); committed witness + narrowing row + sibling corpora on all three enum tests | `TestRV3W_M4_ProofKindSiblingNamesRefused` (fails under the sibling-admitting mutant at both entries) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-proof-sibling.log` |\n38|| P3-5: partial-progress create member unstated | TRACEABILITY bound only: the interim-proven member refuses uncertain with the key parked; exit route `unavailable → terminate-stale` (final leaf); the absent-proven member resumes | — (bound, not behavior; characterized by the reviewer's `TestRV3_PartialCreateProgressIsNotResumable` probe) | TRACEABILITY.md stated bounds |\n39|| Retired `N-fencing-epoch-only` | Harness-only: provably equivalent post-fix (proof in TRACEABILITY mutant-table intro) — a stale_owner park implies a decided-stale verdict over the same observation and both arms call `fenceLive` with the same refusal, so no test can distinguish the weakened park arm | — (retired; the mismatch fact stays measured by `N-fencing-verdict-winner` + the losing-lease members of `TestRV3F3_GrantLessStaleFences`) | TRACEABILITY.md mutant table |\n40|| Re-keyed `N-fencing-operation` | Harness-only: same plant (direct question through `mutation`), new killer `TestObserveFencingNonLiveSourcesLeaveState` — the launch-class requirement now shows on the surfaced park vocabulary | `TestObserveFencingNonLiveSourcesLeaveState` (fails under the plant: hard refusal instead of the stale_owner park) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-fencing-operation.log` |\n41|\n42|Reviewer-mutant mirrors: all five surviving rev3 reviewer narrowings\n43|(RV3-M1/M2/M3/M4/M8) are mirrored as committed harness rows with\n44|committed killers (`N-engine-recheck-auth-expiry`,\n45|`N-result-evidence-bound`, `N-engine-conditional-disposition`,\n46|`N-proof-sibling`, `N-status-last-operation-empty`); RV3-M6/M7 were\n47|already killed by the committed suite. The three reviewer controls\n48|map to the existing `N-auth-epoch-low` kill, build-break ERROR\n49|detection, and the `C-control` SURVIVED control.\n50|\n51|## F3: members enumerated and why the enumeration is complete\n52|\n53|The stale class is factored into three questions: (1) which\n54|observations REACH the verdict, (2) which tuples the verdict calls\n55|stale, (3) which sources fence.\n56|\n57|(1) The verdict is consulted on every non-park outcome of the direct\n58|question. For a stale tuple over a verified well-formed winner, the\n59|only `Authorize` outcomes that are not a stale/remote park are the\n60|four grant-precondition refusals — no grant, no clock reading,\n61|lapsed grant, unusable policy — because the ownership arms all pass\n62|by construction and these are all four refusals the gate can surface\n63|after them (gate arms at `gate.go:338–349`, in order). All four are\n64|driven to fence from active/parked/quiescing under local AND remote\n65|winners (the grant arms precede direction, so a remote winner with\n66|no grant refuses grant-gated rather than parking remote — the\n67|fallback covers it at the first question). The relative question\n68|needs no fallback: it carries the direct observation's grant facts\n69|unchanged and the grant arms do not read `LocalHostID`, so a direct\n70|remote park implies the relative question passes the grant arms.\n71|Completeness is structural: the verdict never consults\n72|grant/clock/policy, so no fifth grant member can hide behind it.\n73|\n74|(2) Decided-stale (older epoch, same-epoch lease mismatch) fences;\n75|decided-not-stale (winning tuple, future epoch) and undecidable\n76|(malformed presented/session/epoch/lease, session mismatch, no\n77|winner, malformed winner, unverified, ambiguous, failed handoff —\n78|the gate's pre-grant arms mirrored one by one) surface the refusal\n79|with no transition. The failed-handoff park is deliberately\n80|preserved: handoff history is ownership, not a grant precondition.\n81|\n82|(3) Creating fences grant-less with the other live states;\n83|absent/stopped/stale_fenced/unavailable surface the grant refusal\n84|(local and remote).\n85|\n86|## E3: members enumerated and why the enumeration is complete\n87|\n88|The per-effect authorization recheck has three axes: kind binding,\n89|expiry, and the lease tuple. The kind axis is fixed per operation\n90|(no mid-operation rotation is expressible — the context carries one\n91|kind); the tuple axis was pinned at positions 1–3 in rev3\n92|(`N-engine-recheck-auth`, `-third`); the expiry axis is pinned here\n93|at the second stop effect with the deadline still ahead\n94|(`TestRV3W_M1`, killed by `N-engine-recheck-auth-expiry`, which keeps\n95|the tuple recheck per-effect and freezes only the expiry instant).\n96|The generation recheck has one axis and was pinned at the same\n97|positions. The E1 `expired` members now kill on the receipt as well:\n98|with the deadline past the expiry, an entry-exempting mutant binds\n99|the receipt before the recheck refuses, so only the receipt\n100|assertion distinguishes it (all three create subtests kill on\n101|`Lookup found a receipt`, verified by hand-applying the mutant).\n102|\n103|## AC coverage: 93 of 93 rows driven\n104|\n105|Measured, not restated: 93 data rows counted in\n106|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md` (rows 1–84 keep rev3 numbers;\n107|rows 85–93 are the rework rows), 109 cited top-level tests all\n108|present via `go test -list` (107 in-package + the fencing agreement\n109|test + the `terminalbackend` column test), every cited subtest\n110|`--- PASS`, zero missing (see `ratio-check.log`); the full package\n111|suite is green (`terminstance-test-v.log`: exit 0, 111 `--- PASS`,\n112|0 `--- FAIL` — the 4 in-package tests not cited in the matrix are\n113|supporting positive/store-level pins, as in rev3). Production call\n114|sites are named per row in the matrix and per clause in TRACEABILITY.md.\n115|The five `internal/fencing` verdict tests are the verdict's own\n116|contract (`fencing-test-v.log`: exit 0, 47 `--- PASS`); every verdict\n117|arm is additionally killed through `ObserveFencing`, so the\n118|composition — not the helper — is measured.\n119|\n120|## Negative and mutant evidence\n121|\n122|- `mutant_harness.py`: 116/116 rows match on two full passes with\n123|  identical verdict lists — 114 narrowing KILLED + 1 tightening edge\n124|  KILLED + the SURVIVED control. The tightening row\n125|  (`N-auth-epoch-high`) is unchanged and documented; the retired row\n126|  (`N-fencing-epoch-only`) is documented with its equivalence proof.\n127|  Per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in `mutants/pass1/` and\n128|  `mutants/pass2/` (116 plants each, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no\n129|  `__pycache__`); production blobs verified byte-identical\n130|  before/after/across passes (`blob-*.txt`, covering\n131|  `internal/terminstance/*.go` and `internal/fencing/staleness.go`).\n132|- Crash/idempotency: carried from rev3 (no new durable write — the\n133|  verdict and the recheck are pure over their inputs, and the\n134|  evidence-bound/disposition/grammar arms are pure gates). The rev3\n135|  no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL evidence on both the\n136|  quiesce and create seams stands unchanged.\n137|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects\n138|  source text. (`TestRV3_FencingNoLocalTupleComparison` is a\n139|  composition pin, not a gate: it asserts the absence of tuple\n140|  references in `fencing.go`, and the verdict rows measure the\n141|  composed behavior through the entry.)\n142|\n143|## Validation suite (configured commands, in order)\n144|\n145|Every command below is quoted from `task-board.config.json`\n146|`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (30 commands) and was\n147|executed once against the exact candidate tree; logs in `cmd/`.\n148|Command 5 ran as 4 bounded chunks with identical flags (packages\n149|1–10/11–20/21–30/31–40; each package exactly once, no flags\n150|shortened) because a single shell call is time-bounded; see\n151|`cmd05-summary.txt` and `cmd05-r1..r4.log`.\n152|\n153|| # | Command | Exit |\n154|| --- | --- | --- |\n155|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\"` | 0 |\n156|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n157|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n158|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 (40/40 packages ok) |\n159|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | 0 (4 chunks, 40/40, 0 DATA RACE) |\n160|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 (40/40; terminstance 86.0%, fencing 97.8%) |\n161|| 7–10 | rpcwire fuzz ×4 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×4 |\n162|| 11 | scalar fuzz ×1 | 0 |\n163|| 12–15 | canonicaljson fuzz ×4 | 0 ×4 |\n164|| 16–23 | secconftest fuzz ×8 | 0 ×8 |\n165|| 24 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (contracts=64, cases=140, clauses 56/569 — trunk figures unchanged) |\n166|| 25 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0, tree unmodified |\n167|| 26 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n168|| 27 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n169|| 28 | `git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` | 0 |\n170|| 29 | `task-board validate` | 0 (zero issues name this task or story) |\n171|| 30 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n172|\n173|An extra `GOOS=windows go vet` of the touched packages also exits 0\n174|(`cmd27b-windows-vet.log`; not a configured command). The `.go` tree\n175|was verified byte-identical before and after the race gate\n176|(`go-sha-before-race.txt` == `go-sha-after-race.txt`), so the race\n177|ran against the exact candidate.\n178|\n179|## Files changed (rev4 delta on top of the rev3 tree)\n180|\n181|- `internal/fencing/staleness.go` (new): exported\n182|  `StaleRelativeToWinner` verdict; `staleness_test.go` (new): tuple\n183|  arms, grant-independence, remote direction, undecided members,\n184|  gate agreement; `doc.go`: one verdict sentence. Nothing else in\n185|  the landed package is touched.\n186|- `internal/terminstance/fencing.go`: verdict fallback composition\n187|  + doc; `fencing_grantless_test.go` (new): 48-transition regression\n188|  test, decided-not-stale keeps, 9-member undecided keeps,\n189|  non-live verdict-path pins; `review_witness_test.go` (new): the\n190|  five reviewer witnesses verbatim + the no-local-tuple\n191|  composition pin.\n192|- `internal/terminstance/`: late-deadline fixture\n193|  (`fixtureLateDeadline`, `fixturePastExpiry`,\n194|  `testContextWithDeadline`, `testCreateContextWithDeadline`) with\n195|  both E1 expired members re-keyed to kill on the receipt;\n196|  sibling-vocabulary corpora on all three enum tests;\n197|  `mutant_harness.py` 100 → 116 rows (17 new, 1 retired, 1\n198|  re-keyed); `TRACEABILITY.md` 84 → 93 rows.\n199|- `README.md`: grant-less fencing sentence, §13.7 scope, battery\n200|  count 98 → 114 narrowing rows.\n201|- `LOGBOOK.md`: rev4 rework entry (additive, newest-first).\n202|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n203|\n204|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n205|\n206|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added. All\n207|rev3 bounds stand. Newly stated: the interim-proven create member\n208|refuses uncertain with the key parked and exits only through the\n209|final leaf's `unavailable → terminate-stale` path (P3-5); the\n210|failed-handoff park is preserved by the verdict (ownership history,\n211|not a grant precondition); the retired row's equivalence (a stale\n212|park implies a decided-stale verdict) with its proof. The per-code\n213|disposition mapping and the AX-side seam emission codes remain the\n214|leaf's contract where the spec pins the vocabulary but not the\n215|mapping.\n216|\n217|## Handoff\n218|\n219|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n220|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n221|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`,\n222|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md`,\n223|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
