{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c659","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":391,"recorded_at":1780531400000777,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b35e-e04a-77a1-9ee8-1a3dabb64869"},"task_id":"01a0b35e-e04a-77a1-9ee8-1a3dabb64869","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b35e-e04a-77a1-9ee8-1a3dabb64869","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1062 line(s) above)\n1063|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1064|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1065|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1066|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1067|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1068|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1069|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1070|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1071|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1072|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1073|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1074|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1075|\n1076|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1077|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1078|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1079|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1080|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1081|\n1082|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1083|\n1084|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1085|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1086|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1087|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1088|\n1089|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1090|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1091|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1092|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1093|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1094|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1095|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1096|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1097|\n1098|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1099|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1100|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1101|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1102|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1103|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1104|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1105|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1106|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1107|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1108|\n1109|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1110|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1111|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1112|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1113|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1114|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1115|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1116|\n1117|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1118|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1119|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1120|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1121|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1122|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1123|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1124|\n1125|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1126|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1127|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1128|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1129|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1130|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1131|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1132|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1133|\n1134|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1135|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1136|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1137|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1138|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1139|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1140|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1141|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1142|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1143|\n1144|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1145|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1146|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1147|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1148|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1149|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1150|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1151|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1152|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1153|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1154|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1155|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1156|\n1157|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1158|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1159|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1160|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1161|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1162|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1163|persisted or replicated.\n1164|\n1165|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1166|| --- | --- | --- |\n1167|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1168|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1169|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1170|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1171|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1172|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1173|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1174|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1175|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1176|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1177|\n1178|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1179|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1180|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1181|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1182|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
