{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c737","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":502,"recorded_at":1780531400000999,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b35f-0920-7f32-a0bf-4ea6df739b9c"},"task_id":"01a0b35f-0920-7f32-a0bf-4ea6df739b9c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b35f-0920-7f32-a0bf-4ea6df739b9c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/doc.go`.\n1|// Package axpane implements the validation core of the\n2|// `ax pane SESSION_ID` enforcement wrapper: the decision every managed\n3|// pane runs before launching, reattaching, offering, parking, or\n4|// refusing a provider.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.B (Terminal Backend\n7|// Manifest/Probe identity through the landed terminalbackend registry\n8|// and contract), Section 4.C/4.1/4.2 (the wrapper rule: validate\n9|// configuration, load the logical session, synchronize known lease\n10|// records when possible, compare the local fencing token before\n11|// launching a provider, park safely when ownership is remote,\n12|// ambiguous, or unverified; the after-restore sequence 1-5; terminal\n13|// creation and the wrapper's first child start idempotent on\n14|// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) with one receipt per pair;\n15|// no credential-dependent tmux server creation from a background\n16|// caller; a cached sentinel or managername observation never\n17|// authorizes resume), Section 4.D (closed capabilities and\n18|// evidence: only the exact admitted capability rows authorize an\n19|// action), Section 5.2 Terminal Events (session.parked with its\n20|// reason vocabulary, terminal.created and session.resumed v4\n21|// terminal binding/evidence payloads), Section 5.7 (the newest\n22|// published checkpoint through the chain fold), Section 7.A\n23|// (Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding descriptor),\n24|// and Section 13.1 Direct-session launch steps 3-4 (durable terminal\n25|// entry with the bootstrap operation ID, then provider launch with\n26|// its validated argv/env plan).\n27|//\n28|// Division of authority (composed, not forked): every check is\n29|// composed from a landed gate. Owner epoch and fencing come from\n30|// internal/fencing (AuthorizeActivation, AuthorizeRestore for the\n31|// decision, AuthorizeMutation for every event emission, the sealed\n32|// LeaseToken projection, the parked vocabulary); materialization\n33|// validity from internal/matjournal (Store.Get with its grammar and\n34|// cross-reference validation plus the committed-phase and\n35|// fold-newest-source rules this package states) and checkpoint\n36|// admission from internal/sessckpt (Get, which re-attests) with\n37|// internal/sessrepo attestation (AttestCheckpointRecord) plus the\n38|// fold-newest and session bindings this package states, and the\n39|// one successor-lease implication (a checkpoint-carrying winner\n40|// means the fold published a newest) asserted after fencing; the\n41|// effective persisted profile from internal/sessprofile\n42|// (DecodeRecord, DecodeEvent, Derive, DeriveForHeads) with Section\n43|// 7.7 mapping refusals from internal/provhost (ResolveMapping,\n44|// profile_mapping_unavailable); provider identity from\n45|// internal/provhost (CheckResumeTuple, VerifyIdentityBuild,\n46|// VerifyIdentityDiscovery) with internal/resumesmoke evidence\n47|// (VerifyRecord) as a precondition input; backend identity from\n48|// internal/terminalbackend (ParseManifest, ParseProbe,\n49|// ParseEvidence, GenerationDigest, Reconcile,\n50|// CapabilitiesForOperation via CheckOperation, CheckEntrypoint,\n51|// AdmitProviderDescriptor); lifecycle foldability from\n52|// internal/sessstate (DecodeRecord, DecodeEvent, Reduce over the\n53|// §5.7 table for lifecycle foldability and the newest published\n54|// checkpoint); configuration validity from internal/config (Load);\n55|// session, lease, and event durability from internal/sessrepo\n56|// (GetRecord, ListEvents, fencing.Observe over ListLeases,\n57|// AppendEvent); refusal shapes from internal/axerror\n58|// (NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable for the credential-conditional\n59|// capability_unavailable with typed realm/readiness details,\n60|// NewTargetAuthMissing for the smoke precondition).\n61|// ParkedPayload and the evidence-ID pre-checks restate closed-shape\n62|// predicates the canonicaljson owner re-enforces at AppendEvent:\n63|// fail-fast input guards, not a second shape model.\n64|//\n65|// The pure core is Decide: exactly one of\n66|// launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked(reason)|\n67|// refused(class). Arm order is precedence and is pinned by the\n68|// decision table: configuration, session, bootstrap idempotency\n69|// with the window predicate, backend identity and capability\n70|// admission with the headless conditional, fencing (activation or\n71|// restore entry), the successor-lease null-fold arm,\n72|// materialization with the fold-newest source binding, checkpoint\n73|// bound to the fold newest and session, provider identity,\n74|// provider-auth smoke with the target binding, realm evidence,\n75|// profile derivation from the checkpoint closure on resume and\n76|// mapping, entrypoint, provider descriptor, then the outcome\n77|// selection (reattach on the recorded pair, remote attach/takeover\n78|// offer for interactive remote owners, parked in all other remote\n79|// cases, launch).\n80|//\n81|// Durable state: the bootstrap binding store (binding.go) binds\n82|// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) to the one recorded\n83|// wrapper/child before any launch side effect under the landed\n84|// no-replace + fsync discipline with crash hooks: the session's\n85|// first binding anchors the in-window contention, and every\n86|// recorded pair keeps its own receipt, so post-window pairs\n87|// record alongside — never over — their superseded receipts. It\n88|// never persists or replicates a PID: identity is the\n89|// AX-allocated UUIDv7 terminal instance ID plus the binding\n90|// digest. Parked decisions with a locally held, verified winner\n91|// and a foldable lifecycle author through sessrepo.AppendEvent\n92|// under the winning lease (events.go); remote, unverifiable, or\n93|// unfolderable parks carry no chain event rather than\n94|// manufacturing a collision.\n95|//\n96|// Bounds: no `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no\n97|// provider process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n98|// broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive as\n99|// Decide inputs) and later leaves. The mesh lease refresh of\n100|// after-restore step 2 is a caller-reported fact (Verified), not a\n101|// network call. Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n102|// terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier.\n103|package axpane","final_result":true}}}
