{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c80f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":610,"recorded_at":1780531400001215,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b35f-5064-7270-9b2f-cff34ba49de6"},"task_id":"01a0b35f-5064-7270-9b2f-cff34ba49de6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b35f-5064-7270-9b2f-cff34ba49de6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# internal/terminstance — TRACEABILITY\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §4.B (generation bound),\n4|§4.C (lifecycle and operations), §4.D (capability conditionals), §5.2\n5|(status/unknown discipline), §7.A (descriptor generation binding, cited\n6|landed), §13.1 (durable terminal entry before provider launch), §13.7\n7|(cold force takeover: the prior owner is stale when it learns the\n8|winner). Every\n9|row names the production entry and the committed test that drives it;\n10|every expectation asserts the literal specification token at the entry.\n11|Coverage: **93 of 93 AC rows driven** (counted below; verified by\n12|`go test ./internal/terminstance/ -count=1 -v`). Rows 73–84 are the\n13|rev3 rework rows (recovery resumption, remote-winner fencing, create\n14|gates, recheck positions, session axes, deadline instants, kind\n15|negatives, landed kind delegation, store pre/post-link); rows 85–93\n16|are the rev4 rework rows (grant-less fencing verdict, expiry recheck,\n17|evidence edge, conditional disposition, proof siblings, last-operation\n18|grammar). Rows 1–84 keep their numbers; rows 46–48's grant-less and\n19|expiry gaps (rev3 review) are closed by rows 85–89.\n20|\n21|## Landed extensions\n22|\n23|Every addition extends a landed type or gate; nothing is forked:\n24|\n25|| Addition | Extends |\n26|| --- | --- |\n27|| `ParseAXAuthorization`, `CheckAuthorization` | `terminalbackend.ParseAttachAuthorization` twin (shape discipline, strict expiry, binding checks); frame and member grammars delegated to `environ`/`scalar` |\n28|| `ParseRetryDisposition`, `DispositionFor` | New leaf contract over the landed row-code vocabulary (`terminalbackend` code consts aliased, never retyped) |\n29|| `ParseProviderProofKind`, `RequiresProviderObservation` | New leaf contract over the §4.C proof vocabulary |\n30|| `ParseMutationContext`, `CheckMutationContext`, `KeySegments` | `terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey` shapes, `ParseID`, `CheckVersionTuple`, `GenerationDigest` |\n31|| `ParseOperationBody`, `ParseStatusBody` | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` closed-shape discipline |\n32|| `Result`, `CheckResult` | `terminalbackend` state/effect vocabularies, `scalar` digests |\n33|| `Engine.ExecuteMutating`, `ExecuteStatus` | `terminalbackend.CheckTransition`, `CheckErrorAllowed`, `CheckOperation`, `CheckStatusResult`; uncertain retries reconcile through `ExecuteStatus` itself (no second status path) |\n34|| `kindFor` | `terminalbackend.TransitionAuthorization` (landed authorization column; the engine honors create/control, no restated table) |\n35|| `ReceiptStore` | `terminalbackend.Receipt`/`Ledger`/`ImportLedger` triple and line encoding (byte-agreed, crash-durable) |\n36|| `ObserveFencing` | `fencing.Authorize` + `ParkDetails` asked twice (present token, then relative-to-winner from the winner's host), plus the landed `fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner` verdict for grant-gated refusals; stale verdict only; no local tuple comparison; live sources only |\n37|| Engine error codes | `terminalbackend` code consts aliased; the four literals the landed core spells only inside its allowed-error table (`terminal_backend_timeout`, `terminal_backend_process_failed`, `quiesce_timeout`, `stop_timeout`) pinned admitted by `TestRowCodesAreAdmittedByCheckErrorAllowed` |\n38|\n39|## AC rows\n40|\n41|### AXAuthorization (item 1) — `ParseAXAuthorization`, `CheckAuthorization`\n42|\n43|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n44|| --- | --- | --- |\n45|| 1 | Closed 7-member object admitted, every member literal | `TestParseAXAuthorizationAdmitsClosedFixture` |\n46|| 2 | lease_id is UUIDv4 (v7, garbage, number refuse) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n47|| 3 | lease_epoch 1 admitted | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n48|| 4 | lease_epoch 9007199254740991 admitted | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n49|| 5 | lease_epoch 0 refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n50|| 6 | lease_epoch 9007199254740992 refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n51|| 7 | Epoch AX number model (fraction, exponent, sign, string, bool, null, huge refuse) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochNumberModel` |\n52|| 8 | holder_host_id is UUIDv7 | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n53|| 9 | authorization_kind closed create/control/force_stale/restore | `TestParseAXAuthorizationKindClosed` |\n54|| 10 | Strict expiry (equal and inverted refuse unauthorized) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationStrictExpiry` |\n55|| 11 | authorization_evidence_id is a digest | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n56|| 12 | Unknown member refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n57|| 13 | Missing member refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n58|| 14 | Frame violations (non-object, trailing, duplicate, surrogate, non-UTF8) refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n59|| 15 | Kind binding (control presented as create refuses) | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/kind_mismatch` |\n60|| 16 | Expiry at and past the edge refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/expired`, `/expiry_edge_refuses` |\n61|| 17 | Lease identity drift refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_identity_drift` |\n62|| 18 | Lease epoch drift refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/l