rcesLeaveState` |\n296|| N-engine-timeout-code-stop | Row timeout code (stop reports quiesce code) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/request-stop` |\n297|| N-engine-timeout-code-default | Row timeout code (default reports stop code) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/quiesce-input` |\n298|| N-engine-status-source | Status source matrix (garbage admitted) | `TestExecuteStatusAllSources` |\n299|| N-params-bootstrap | Params bootstrap (admits nope) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n300|| N-params-quiescence-quiesce | Params quiescence quiesce-arm (admits nope) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n301|| N-params-quiescence-wait | Params quiescence wait-arm (admits nope) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n302|| N-params-proof | Params proof (admits provider_restart) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n303|| N-params-evidence | Params stop evidence (admits not-a-digest) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n304|| N-params-graceful | Params graceful bound (admits 3600001) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n305|| N-version-delegation | Version-tuple delegation (fixture backend skips) | `TestParseMutationContextMemberRefusals` |\n306|| N-body-scope | Body scope map (admits create) | `TestParseOperationBodyScopeGate` |\n307|| N-body-members | Body member set (admits one extra) | `TestParseOperationBodyRefusals` |\n308|| N-store-sweep-age | Sweep age gate (sweeps live-suffixed young staging) | `TestStoreSweepKeepsLiveStaging` |\n309|| N-result-effects-sort | Effects wire order (inverted) | `TestBuildResultSortsEffectsAndEvidence` |\n310|| N-result-evidence-sort | Evidence wire order (inverted) | `TestBuildResultSortsEffectsAndEvidence` |\n311|| N-fencing-verdict-future | Verdict epoch arm (future admitted as stale) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessDecidedNotStaleLeavesState/future_epoch` |\n312|| N-fencing-verdict-winner | Verdict lease arm (winning lease admitted as stale) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessDecidedNotStaleLeavesState/winning_token` |\n313|| N-fencing-verdict-unverified | Verdict verified arm (epoch-1 unverified decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/unverified` |\n314|| N-fencing-verdict-ambiguous | Verdict ambiguity arm (epoch-1 ambiguous decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/ambiguous` |\n315|| N-fencing-verdict-nowinner | Verdict winner arm (epoch-1 winnerless decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/no_winner` |\n316|| N-fencing-verdict-winner-shape | Verdict winner-shape arm (epoch-1 malformed winner decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/malformed_winner` |\n317|| N-fencing-verdict-session | Verdict session arm (epoch-1 mismatch decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/session_mismatch` |\n318|| N-fencing-verdict-handoff | Verdict handoff arm (epoch-1 failed handoff decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/failed_handoff` |\n319|| N-fencing-verdict-presented-session | Verdict session-grammar arm (agreed-malformed decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/malformed_session` |\n320|| N-fencing-verdict-presented-epoch | Verdict epoch-zero arm (losing-lease zero decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/epoch_zero` |\n321|| N-fencing-verdict-presented-lease | Verdict lease-grammar arm (epoch-1 malformed lease decided) | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessUndecidedLeavesState/malformed_lease` |\n322|| N-fencing-verdict-composition | Composition fences on decided alone | `TestRV3F3_GrantLessDecidedNotStaleLeavesState` |\n323|| N-engine-recheck-auth-expiry | Per-effect expiry recheck dropped (tuple stays) | `TestRV3W_M1_AuthExpiryRecheckedBeforeEachEffect` |\n324|| N-result-evidence-bound | Evidence bound admits 257 (both surfaces) | `TestRV3W_M2_EvidenceBoundEdge` |\n325|| N-engine-conditional-disposition | Conditional arm reports status_first | `TestRV3W_M3_ConditionalCapabilityDisposition` |\n326|| N-proof-sibling | Proof vocabulary admits the capability name | `TestRV3W_M4_ProofKindSiblingNamesRefused` |\n327|| N-status-last-operation-empty | Status admits empty last_operation_id | `TestRV3W_M8_StatusLastOperationGrammar` |\n328|| C-control | Comment-only control (SURVIVED) | `TestRequiresProviderObservation` |\n329|\n330|## Stated bounds\n331|\n332|- No `ax` command, no doctor result, no runtime capability claim: the\n333|  `Backend` interface is modeled; tmux/ConPTY/process control and the\n334|  provider process do not exist here.\n335|- Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed-object parsing: no parser\n336|  exists on trunk (`canonicaljson` explicitly rejects\n337|  `urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding`); the generation bound is\n338|  enforced on the surfaces this leaf owns and cited landed for the\n339|  Provider Protocol 3 descriptor (`terminalbackend` checkGeneration\n340|  arms). Full Binding parsing belongs with the provisioning surface.\n341|- CLI Result 4 summary: no landed Result 4 body carries a raw\n342|  generation member (`internal/cliresult` carries none by grep), so\n343|  there is no surface to witness the bound on; consistent with §4.E\n344|  (generation is host-local, non-replicable).\n345|- Attach, restore, terminate-stale, manifest, probe: refused by the\n346|  engine and body scope gates. Restore/terminate-stale recovery and\n347|  terminal binding events belong to the story's final leaf.\n348|- Create is receipt-scoped: receipt, transition, target and headless\n349|  rules execute; the full create body (Binding, Entrypoint,\n350|  presentation transport) belongs to provisioning.\n351|- Credential-realm conditional: credential need is not modeled on the\n352|  engine path.\n353|- Protocol_version membership in the admitted probe list is enforced at\n354|  registry admission (landed), not re-derived per operation; the\n355|  operation gate enforces grammar plus major 1 through the landed\n356|  `CheckVersionTuple` arms.\n357|- The per-code disposition mapping is the leaf's contract where the\n358|  spec pins the vocabulary but not the mapping; every arm is pinned\n359|  literally and mutated. In particular a lease rotation after a\n360|  committed effect reports `after=unavailable` with\n361|  `new_authorization` (the lease names its own remedy even though the\n362|  caller likely needs a status read too); §4.C's only sentence about\n363|  `unavailable` pairs it with `status_first`, so this pairing is the\n364|  leaf's stated contract, recorded as a literal tension, not a defect.\n365|- `holder_host_id` is parsed (UUIDv7) and never bound:\n366|  `CheckAuthorization` compares the §5.3 winning (lease_id, epoch)\n367|  tuple only, so a foreign holder under the winning tuple is\n368|  admitted. No path mints authority from the holder member.\n369|- Resumption re-issues effects under the SAME idempotency key and\n370|  relies on the backend's own key binding for safety (§4.C: \"AX and\n371|  backend durably bind the pair before the first child side effect\";\n372|  §13.13 safe_retry): the engine never issues one logical operation\n373|  under a second key, so no second process is allocated. For\n374|  wait-safe-boundary the source is the target, so a proven quiescing\n375|  resumes and the resumed observation supersedes any lost one; at\n376|  most one completion exists per key either way (no-replace).\n377|- A same-key retry that reconciles to the proven TARGET (or closed)\n378|  refuses uncertain rather than replaying: the effects may have\n379|  committed but their evidence cannot be proven, and re-issuing from\n380|  a non-source observation would violate the transition matrix. The\n381|  row recovery columns (\"then same-key retry only if not closed\")\n382|  are implemented as proceed-iff-source-proven. The interim-proven\n383|  member of the create recovery (P3-5): a receipt without completion\n384|  after `binding_persisted` committed, with status reporting the\n385|  interim `creating` and identity match, refuses uncertain and the\n386|  key stays parked — the partial progress is reachable only through\n387|  the `unavailable → terminate-stale` path of the story's final\n388|  leaf. The absent-proven member instead resumes: the retry\n389|  re-performs both effects under the same receipt with one\n390|  completion and one receipt (no second binding).\n391|- AX-side seam emissions are outside the §4.C row sets: the row sets\n392|  govern backend reports (gated through the landed\n393|  `CheckErrorAllowed`), while an uncoded effect outcome classifies\n394|  `terminal_backend_process_failed` and an uncertain retry refuses\n395|  `terminal_backend_unavailable`, both with after `unavailable` and\n396|  `status_first` per the row recovery columns. Engine deadline\n397|  cancels before any attempt report `replay_same` on every row\n398|  (nothing was attempted); a backend-reported `stop_timeout` maps\n399|  through `DispositionFor` (`status_first` even uncommitted) because\n400|  the graceful wait ran. The two stop directions are pinned together\n401|  (`TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes`,\n402|  `TestExecuteBackendRowErrorSets`).\n403|- The wait/stop \"lesser of request deadline and timeout\" bound is\n404|  enforced by the backend wait (modeled here), which reports a coded\n405|  `quiesce_timeout`/`stop_timeout` proving non-commit; the engine\n406|  validates the timeout members (`uint53[1..3600000]`, carried in\n407|  `Params`) and enforces the `MutationContext` deadline.\n408|- Document member arms delegate their grammars to the landed\n409|  `environ`/`scalar` owners and are pinned literally through the\n410|  parse entries; where a Go-level twin re-validates with the same\n411|  detail, the Go twin carries the narrowing row (a document-side\n412|  weakening alone is masked by the twin). The body scope gate and\n413|  the body member-set gate have no twin and carry their own rows\n414|  (`N-body-scope`, `N-body-members`). The engine scope gate is\n415|  fail-fast ordering: admitting an operation past it is masked by\n416|  the `checkParams`/`KeySegments` scope defaults firing the same\n417|  detail (defense in depth, stated); `kindFor` is not redundant and\n418|  carries `N-engine-kind-map`.\n419|- The fencing operation must be launch-class (`restore`, equivalent\n420|  to `activation` on the stale arms and chosen for the terminal\n421|  domain); the non-launch entries refuse stale tokens instead of\n422|  parking them, measured by `N-fencing-operation` on the direct\n423|  question and `N-fencing-operation-remote` on the relative question.\n424|  The relative question re-authorizes from the winner's own host; it\n425|  composes the landed gate (no local tuple comparison) and fences\n426|  only on the relative stale verdict from a live source. Grant-gated\n427|  refusals (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable\n428|  policy — the complete grant-precondition class, since these are all\n429|  four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms\n430|  pass) consult the landed `StaleRelativeToWinner` verdict instead:\n431|  decided-stale fences from a live source, decided-not-stale and\n432|  undecidable surface the refusal. The relative question needs no\n433|  fallback (it carries the direct grant facts unchanged and the grant\n434|  arms do not read `LocalHostID`), and the failed-handoff park is\n435|  preserved (ownership history, not a grant precondition).\n436|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract; the final\n437|  leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin.\n438|\n439|## Inherited advisories (predecessor P3, for the record)\n440|\n441|- P3-6 closed by this leaf: the `Decision.Descriptor` doc in\n442|  `internal/axpane/decide.go` now states the recorded Binding\n443|  terminal instance ID is authoritative on reattach; this package's\n444|  `doc.go` states the consumer side.\n445|- P3-2 bound stated: this leaf adds no I/O-free `Decide` caller (the\n446|  engine never calls `Decide`), so the missing-closure input shape is\n447|  unreachable from this package; the pure-core hardening stays with\n448|  the owner.\n449|- P3-3 bound stated: this leaf never loads checkpoints (no\n450|  `LoadCheckpoint` caller), so the absent-store shape is unreachable\n451|  from this package.\n452|- P3-1, P3-4, P3-5 left to the final leaf (TASK-260830-2056mm):\n453|  journal-only restore closure (recovery domain), `EmitParked`\n454|  winner binding (events domain) and the corrupt-blob negative\n455|  (recovery domain) belong to events-and-recovery work.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
