{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c841","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":635,"recorded_at":1780531400001265,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b35f-6898-7d62-b6fa-5523f60bdb0e"},"task_id":"01a0b35f-6898-7d62-b6fa-5523f60bdb0e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b35f-6898-7d62-b6fa-5523f60bdb0e","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.5.0, commit\n4|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`, worked against the\n5|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` headings named below (byte-identical\n6|to v0.6.0 in these sections). Primary scope is Sections 4.B-4.D,\n7|4.1-4.2, 5.2 Terminal Events, 5.7 (newest checkpoint), 7.A, and\n8|13.1, plus the 2.4 profile authority the wrapper composes. This\n9|file records implementation evidence; per the Story contract the\n10|`internal/traceability` ownership registry is untouched in this\n11|first leaf — the Story's final leaf carries the registry bindings\n12|and re-pin. This package claims no public CLI delivery: no `ax`\n13|command exists in this tree.\n14|\n15|The wrapper validation core (`internal/axpane`) composes every\n16|check from a landed gate and re-implements none: owner epoch and\n17|fencing from `fencing` (`AuthorizeActivation`, `AuthorizeRestore`,\n18|the sealed `LeaseToken`, the parked vocabulary); the authoritative\n19|newest checkpoint from `sessstate` (`Reduce` over the record with\n20|its authoritative chain: `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`);\n21|materialization validity from `matjournal` (`Store.Get` with its\n22|grammar and cross-reference validation, plus the stated\n23|committed-phase and fold-newest-source rules) and checkpoint\n24|admission from `sessckpt` (`Get`, which re-attests through\n25|`sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord` on every read) with the identity,\n26|newest, and session bindings in `Decide`, plus the one\n27|successor-lease implication (a checkpoint-carrying winner means the\n28|fold published a newest) asserted once directly after fencing; the\n29|effective persisted profile from `sessprofile` (`DecodeRecord`,\n30|`DecodeEvent`, `Derive`, `DeriveForHeads`) with Section 7.7 mapping\n31|from `provhost` (`ResolveMapping`,\n32|`profile_mapping_unavailable`); provider identity from `provhost`\n33|(`CheckResumeTuple`, `VerifyIdentityBuild`,\n34|`VerifyIdentityDiscovery`, `CreateIdentity` in fixtures) with\n35|`resumesmoke` evidence (`VerifyRecord`) as a precondition input;\n36|backend identity from `terminalbackend` (`ParseManifest`,\n37|`ParseProbe`, `ParseEvidence`, `GenerationDigest`, `Reconcile`,\n38|`CapabilitiesForOperation` via `CheckOperation`, `CheckEntrypoint`,\n39|`AdmitProviderDescriptor`); configuration validity from `config`\n40|(`Load`); session, lease, and event durability from `sessrepo`\n41|(`GetRecord`, `ListEvents`, `ListSessions`, `fencing.Observe` over\n42|`ListLeases`, `AppendEvent`); refusal shapes from `axerror`\n43|(`NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`, `NewTargetAuthMissing`).\n44|\n45|## Acceptance rows\n46|\n47|43 of 43 AC rows are driven at the production entries named below;\n48|the denominator is re-derived by counting this table (43 data\n49|rows), not restated: rev2 claimed \"41 of 41\" while the table has\n50|always held 43 rows, and the independent reviewer measured 39 of\n51|43 faithfully driven. The four unfaithful rev2 rows —\n52|\"Materialization validity gates local resume\", \"Checkpoint\n53|admission gates resume\", \"After-restore sequence 1-5\" (all three\n54|shared the lease-checkpoint keying), and \"Bootstrap idempotency\"\n55|(the superseded receipt) — were re-pinned faithfully in rev3, and\n56|the four rows the rev3 reviewer measured unfaithful (the same\n57|first three, now sharing the strict lease/fold equality, plus\n58|\"Effective profile derived with source\", pinned only for the\n59|epoch-1 owner) are re-pinned faithfully in rev4: the post-takeover\n60|lifecycle launches from the fold's newest with the newest\n61|checkpoint's closure profile in both modes and both profile\n62|directions, the successor null fold parks, and the stale base\n63|parks. 0 of 43 are delivered as a public CLI surface,\n64|which is an explicit caller-integration bound (no `ax` command\n65|exists in this tree), not a gap in the assigned validation\n66|behavior. Process control, mesh transport, provider supervision,\n67|and backend operations belong to modeled callers and later leaves,\n68|which invoke these entries at every required boundary.\n69|\n70|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n71|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n72|| Lower epoch parks or refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_lower_epoch` | Driven: presented epoch 1 under a winning epoch 2 parks `stale_owner` with the winning lease. |\n73|| Same-epoch loser parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_same_epoch_loser` | Driven: the losing lease at the winning epoch parks `stale_owner`. |\n74|| Future epoch parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_future_epoch` | Driven: an epoch beyond the winner parks `restore_policy`. |\n75|| Foreign session refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_foreign_session` | Driven: a token for another session refuses `lease_conflict`. |\n76|| Expired grant refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` → `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_expired_grant` | Driven: a lapsed grant refuses `lease_conflict` on the launch entry. |\n77|| Malformed token refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_malformed_token` | Driven: epoch 0 refuses `invalid_arguments`. |\n78|| Absent winner parks without authority | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Run` skips emission | `TestDecideTable/parked_absent_winner`, `TestRunParkedWithoutWinnerSkipsEmission` | Driven: no winner parks `restore_policy` with an empty lease ID and authors no event, since `session.parked` requires a winning lease. |\n79|| Ambiguous ownership parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_ambiguous` | Driven: conflicting union observations park `restore_policy`. |\n80|| Unverified ownership parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Emit` → `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` refuses | `TestDecideTable/parked_unverified`, `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop/refuses_unverified` | Driven: without a proving lease refresh the wrapper parks `restore_policy` with no chain event — the mutation gate refuses unverified emission. |\n81|| Failed handoff parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Emit` → `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` refuses | `TestDecideTable/parked_failed_handoff`, `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop/refuses_failed_handoff` | Driven: a losing force lease parks `failed_handoff`, never activates and never emits. |\n82|| Remote interactive owner offers attach | `Decide` → `decideParked` + `terminalbackend.CheckOperation(\"attach\")`; `Run` skips remote emission | `TestDecideTable/attach_remote_interactive` | Driven: a remote winning holder with an interactive terminal and an admitted attach capability offers `attach_remote` with no lease mutation and no chain event under the remote lease. |\n83|| Remote owner otherwise parks or offers takeover | `Decide` → `decideParked`; `Run` skips remote emission | `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_noninteractive`, `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_attach_unproven`, `TestRunRemoteNonInteractiveParksWithoutEmission` | Driven: a non-interactive remote owner parks `remote_owner` (§4.2 step 5); an interactive attach-unproven remote owner offers `takeover_offer`. Both start no runtime and author no chain event under the remote lease. |\n84|| Mode selects entry and capability row | `Decide` → `authorize` + `admitBackend` | `TestDecideRestoreRequiresRestoreCapability`, `TestDecideTable/launch_restore_committed_checkpoint` | Driven: restore mode gates through `AuthorizeRestore` and the `restore` row (a restore-admitting, create-denying backend launches); launch mode gates through `AuthorizeActivation` and `create`. |\n85|| Materialization validity gates local resume | `Decide` → `checkMaterialization`; `Run` → `LoadMaterialization` + `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_not_committed`, `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_absent`, `TestDecideMaterializationStaleParks`, `TestDecideJournalNullFoldParks`, `TestRunRestoreCommitted`, `TestRunRestoreMaterializingParks`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks`, `TestDecidePostTakeoverDivergedBaseLaunches`, `TestRunPostTakeoverRestoreLaunchesWithNewestClosure`, `TestRunPostTakeoverStaleBaseParks`, `TestDecideSuccessorNullFoldParks`, `TestRunSuccessorNullFoldParks` | Driven: a required journal must be admitted by the `matjournal` owner, committed, and sourced from the fold's newest published checkpoint — the winning lease's handoff base is never compared; staging, absence, a null fold, or a superseded source parks `restore_policy`. The epoch-1 owner (null lease checkpoint) parks on an unnamed-digest journal and launches on a newest-sourced one; the post-takeover owner (successor lease base C0, fold newest C1) launches on a C1-sourced journal and parks on a C0-sourced one. A checkpoint-carrying winner over a null fold parks at the one implication arm. Fresh launch leaves the requirement unset (§13.1 runs before the journal commits). |\n86|| Checkpoint admission gates resume | `Decide` → `admitCheckpoint` → `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`; `Run` → `LoadCheckpoint` + `LoadNewestCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_inadmissible`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_absent`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_wrong_identity`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_flipped_digest`, `TestDecideCheckpointNotLeaseParks`, `TestDecideForeignCheckpointParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointNullFoldParks`, `TestDecideCheckpointUnpublishedParks`, `TestRunEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint`, `TestRunNullFoldRestoreParks`, `TestDecidePostTakeoverDivergedBaseLaunches`, `TestRunPostTakeoverRestoreLaunchesWithNewestClosure`, `TestRunPostTakeoverStaleBaseParks` | Driven: a required checkpoint must attest through the `sessrepo` owner, match the required digest, equal the fold's newest published checkpoint, and name this session — the winning lease's handoff base is never compared; garbage, absence, identity drift, a null fold, an unpublished checkpoint, a non-newest checkpoint, or a foreign session parks `restore_policy`. The post-takeover owner (successor lease base C0, fold newest C1) launches on C1 and parks on the stale base C0. |\n87|| Effective profile derived with source | `Decide` → `deriveProfile` → `sessprofile.Derive`/`DeriveForHeads`; `Run` → `LoadProfile` + resumed-checkpoint closure | `TestDecideProfileSourcePinsEvent`, `TestDecideYoloMapping`, `TestDecideResumeProfileUsesClosure`, `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored`, `TestRunNoCkptStorePublishedNewestFails`, `TestRunPostTakeoverLaunchCarriesNewestClosureStandardToYolo`, `TestRunPostTakeoverLaunchCarriesNewestClosureYoloToStandard`, `TestRunPostTakeoverRestoreLaunchesWithNewestClosure`, `TestRunNewestAbsentFromStoreFails` | Driven: launch carries the session head (newest authoritative `profile.changed` with that event's digest, or the record value with null source) only on the checkpoint-free path; resume carries the checkpoint actually resumed — the required checkpoint