` | KILLED |\n171|| N-supersede-no-replace | Test pair receipt replaced on the commit race | `TestSupersedeConcurrentSamePairReplays` | KILLED |\n172|| N-parked-reason | Five-letter reasons admitted; vocabulary otherwise closed | `TestParkedPayloadVocabulary` | KILLED |\n173|| N-emit-mutation | Unverified emissions admitted; verified refusals refuse | `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop/refuses_unverified` | KILLED |\n174|| N-emit-losing-epoch | Losing-epoch emissions admitted; same-or-winning-epoch refusals refuse | `TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses` | KILLED |\n175|| N-parked-fold | Unfolderable restore_policy admitted; other unfolderable refuse | `TestEmitParkedUnfoldableRefuses` | KILLED |\n176|| N-run-fold | Run admits unfolderable restore_policy; other still skip | `TestRunParkedUnfoldableSkipsEmission` | KILLED |\n177|| N-run-ckpt-store | Launch-mode runs with a published newest and no store admitted (head pair launches) | `TestRunNoCkptStorePublishedNewestFails` | KILLED |\n178|| N-window-lease-checkpoint | Window closed on the lease record's checkpoint with a null fold | `TestRunWindowLeaseCheckpointNullFoldRefuses` | KILLED |\n179|| N-run-fold-error | Unfoldable chain laundered as a null fold | `TestRunUnfoldableChainFails` | KILLED |\n180|| N-supersede-replay | Post-window replay keeps launch in restore mode | `TestRunPostWindowSamePairRaceReattaches` | KILLED |\n181|| N-identity-session | Foreign fixture session's identity record admitted | `TestDecideIdentityForeignSessionRefuses` | KILLED |\n182|| N-run-newest-absent | Restore-mode runs with the newest absent from the store admitted (head pair launches) | `TestRunNewestAbsentFromStoreFails/restore` | KILLED |\n183|| C-doc-comment | Comment-only control edit | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence` | SURVIVED |\n184|\n185|No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: this package\n186|contains no gate that inspects source text, so the additional\n187|behavioral-suite mutant the evidence contract names for such gates\n188|has no target here. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call in\n189|`checkProviderIdentity` is fail-fast ordering over the same gate\n190|`VerifyIdentityBuild` enforces internally, so weakening it alone is\n191|unobservable by construction; likewise the `admitted.Has` realm\n192|pre-check is fail-fast before the evidence cross-bind, so weakening\n193|it alone is unobservable and the binding mutants cover the gate;\n194|the N-identity-version mutant covers the provider-identity gate as\n195|a whole. The fencing entry selection (`AuthorizeRestore` vs\n196|`AuthorizeActivation`) shares one launch-class core in the\n197|`fencing` owner, so no behavioral delta exists to mutate; the\n198|mode-selected backend capability row carries the mode mutant\n199|(N-backend-op).\n200|\n201|## Crash and idempotency evidence\n202|\n203|The bootstrap binding is the only durable write. Every receipt\n204|installs under the landed discipline: same-directory staging,\n205|0600, fsync, atomic link as the no-replace commit, staging\n206|cleanup, directory fsync (skipped, never faked, on Windows).\n207|Readers see absence or the complete receipt, never a torn prefix.\n208|The session's first binding anchors the in-window contention and\n209|every recorded pair keeps its own receipt, so post-window pairs\n210|record alongside — never over — their superseded receipts; a crash\n211|between the anchor and pair installs converges the pair from the\n212|anchor bytes on retry. Crash hooks arm both boundaries\n213|(`AfterStage` before the commit, `AfterInstall` after it) on both\n214|install paths; the real-kill test\n215|(`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`) SIGKILLs the child between\n216|commit and directory sync and proves the complete binding plus a\n217|converging identical retry. Parked events append through the\n218|`sessrepo` owner, whose own crash evidence stays with that\n219|package; this leaf proves linkage and round-trip only.\n220|\n221|## Stated bounds\n222|\n223|- No `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider\n224|  process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n225|  broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive\n226|  as `Decide` inputs) and later leaves.\n227|- The bounded mesh lease refresh (after-restore step 2) is the\n228|  caller-reported `Verified` fact, not a network call.\n229|- Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n230|  `terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier`; tests authenticate through\n231|  a generated RSA key.\n232|- Backend liveness (`terminal_backend_unavailable` at the\n233|  operation call site) belongs to the later backend-operation\n234|  leaf: no backend operation exists here, so no availability rule\n235|  is invented.\n236|- The host-local `InstanceBinding` the descriptor must match\n237|  arrives from the modeled backend caller; the wrapper proves\n238|  document-to-binding consistency and never mints backend\n239|  bindings.\n240|- The committed-phase rule for a required materialization is the\n241|  wrapper's stated reading of after-restore step 3 (\"the required\n242|  materialization is valid\").\n243|- Invalid materialization or checkpoint on an otherwise winning\n244|  local owner parks `restore_policy` per the literal step-5\n245|  reading (\"enter parked without launching the provider in all\n246|  other cases\"), with the blocking cause in the decision detail.\n247|- Unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments`: the call names\n248|  no logical session. No `unknown_session` wire code is minted.\n249|- The dead-realm refusal mapping applies only when the caller\n250|  needs the realm row and submitted at least one realm evidence\n251|  object that is unusable (expired or bound to a superseded\n252|  generation). With no submitted realm row, or any usable one, a\n253|  reconcile failure keeps its backend class.\n254|- The realm cross-bind accepts when any submitted realm object\n255|  binds this host and build: order-independent by scan, pinned in\n256|  both evidence orders plus the all-foreign refusal.\n257|- Binding the successor lease's handoff base to a checkpoint the\n258|  chain published is the takeover leaf's obligation: this leaf\n259|  asserts only the implication \"a checkpoint-carrying winner means\n260|  the fold published a newest\" (one site, directly after fencing)\n261|  and compares the base against nothing — a diverged base is the\n262|  ordinary post-takeover state, not a refusal.\n263|- The `realmRowUsable` liveness and generation predicate restates\n264|  the reconcile rule as a stated bound: the aggregate `Reconcile`\n265|  error carries no per-object identity (liveness shares the\n266|  generic mismatch code), so no per-row usability verdict can be\n267|  read off it. The copy is classification-only and fail-closed in\n268|  both directions — it selects the refusal class, never admission.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
