e\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.9; no clause of 7.9 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 8 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.12\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/matjournal/recover.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Recover\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"materialization-journal-recovery\\\",\\n  \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unmeasured\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Recover classifies the journal-observable Section 13.12 failure rows (operator interrupt, owner-resume response lost, atomic rename blocked, disk full, task-board import/open/adopt failure before and after the new lease) into the Section 13.13 outcomes, proved by the crashgate conformance harness; the scanner finds no clause line in the table-shaped Section 13.12 so the binding stays unmeasured, and rows owned by sync, lease, provider, bridge, and lifecycle flows (SSH disconnect, quarantine, divergence, quiesce failure, plugin crash, missing bridge, concurrent takeovers, stale owner, corrupt index) belong to their unlanded owners.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.13\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/matjournal/recover.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Recover\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"materialization-journal-recovery\\\",\\n  \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\",\\n  \\\"crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Recover with the crashgate conformance harness discharges 9 of the 11 normative clauses of Section 13.13 (every-boundary injection for checkpoint/journal-observable paths, exactly-one classification, safe_retry meaning, ambiguity rule, no fourth outcome, conformance record contents, two-live-authority and substitution rejection, unfenced-continuation parking); clauses 13.13#4 and 13.13#5 are discharged only for their journal-durable halves because rollback/parked visibility through event, CLI/status, audit, and lifecycle-projection surfaces belongs to unlanded owners, and boundaries owned by lease, terminal, provider, bridge, sync, lifecycle, and clone flows are recorded NOT APPLICABLE with owners rather than injected.\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"13.13#1\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 10250,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"Every implementation MUST inject a crash and a clean process restart at every\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\",\\n    \\\"crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"13.13#2\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 10252,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"After restart, the recovery evaluator MUST classify the operation into exactly\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"13.13#3\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 10257,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"| <code>saf\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.14.5\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateSessionEventV2\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\",\\n  \\\"core-record-identity-validation\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unmeasured\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateSessionEventV2 validates the Section 13.14.5 v2 Session Event shape, which is topically the subject of the section; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 13.14.5, because the section states its obligations as required-member and variant tables rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure how much of the section this binding actually discharges.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.15\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateSessionEventV3\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\",\\n  \\\"core-record-identity-validation\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateSessionEventV3 validates the Section 13.15 event payload shape, but no clause of Section 13.15 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.1\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v070-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog only and performs no Section 13.1 launch lifecycle; the caller-plan planning-role step, the recorded-argv determinism rule and the persisted-extensions bound Section 13.1 requires are unimplemented. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-3fjjtn. The Section 13.1 name-unused precondition is a separate rule: same-second duplicate names at start are refused by STORY-260916-3ustb3, not here.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.10\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"catalog-v070-exact\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog only and performs no Section 13.10 resume or fork lifecycle; the Curator profile re-resolution, the environment-drift comparison and the refuse-by-default rule Section 13.10 requires are unimplemented. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-3aukw3.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 14291,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3573,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
