sion entries; unresolvable evidence proceeds to append. Not counted as any gate's narrowing. [exit 1]\\nok: N-attach-auth-replay: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Skips authorization exactly on the replay path; fresh attaches still authorize. [exit 1]\\nok: N-attach-conflict: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Drops exactly the input half of the conflict conjunction at both the pre-check and the commit-converge comparison; transport conflicts still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-attach-key: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Collapses exactly the client axis of the idempotency key; the instance axis still separates. [exit 1]\\nok: N-attach-transport: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the smoke_signal transport past the enum; the landed vocabulary refusal surfaces instead of this gate's. [exit 1]\\nok: N-binding-generation: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the 257-character generation; length 0 and 258+ still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-binding-identity: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the wrong self-ID fixture; other identity breaks still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-binding-members: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly one extra binding member; missing members and two extras still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-emit-created-v3: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Emits the created payload at v3; the canonical owner refuses the v4 members under the v3 shape. [exit 1]\\nok: N-emit-resumed-v3: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Emits the resumed payload at v3; the canonical owner refuses the v4 members under the v3 shape. [exit 1]\\nok: N-evidence-0: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the empty evidence set past the shape arm; the partition refusal surfaces instead of the bound. [exit 1]\\nok: N-evidence-257: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly 257 evidence IDs past the shape arm; 258 still refuses. [exit 1]\\nok: N-evidence-dup: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly duplicate evidence IDs; inversions still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-evidence-unsorted: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Skips exactly the first-pair order comparison; later inversions still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-identity-endpoint: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the endpoint form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces. [exit 1]\\nok: N-identity-pid: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the PID form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces. [exit 1]\\nok: N-prescan-context: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Skips the context pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-contradiction-absent: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Claims exactly the bound contradiction as absence; matched observations keep their verdicts. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-creating-child: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the creating interim as a child; backend-reported unavailable still parks. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-mismatch: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture changed operation in-window; other changed operations still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-second-child: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Adopts exactly the unbound live instance as a second child; proven absence still vacates. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-status-error: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Launders exactly the status read failure as proven absence; reported observations keep their verdicts. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-window: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Inverts exactly the window bit; post-window changed pairs refuse while in-window proceeds. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-admission: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Swallows exactly the landed drift refusal; every other admission refusal still surfaces. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-binding: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Drops exactly the evidence protocol arm; backend and implementation drift still refuse at this gate. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-identity: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Drops exactly the probe half of the substitution check; manifest and evidence aliases still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-res