 every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces. [exit 1]\\nok: N-identity-pid: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the PID form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces. [exit 1]\\nok: N-prescan-context: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Skips the context pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-contradiction-absent: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Claims exactly the bound contradiction as absence; matched observations keep their verdicts. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-creating-child: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the creating interim as a child; backend-reported unavailable still parks. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-mismatch: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture changed operation in-window; other changed operations still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-second-child: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Adopts exactly the unbound live instance as a second child; proven absence still vacates. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-status-error: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Launders exactly the status read failure as proven absence; reported observations keep their verdicts. [exit 1]\\nok: N-recover-window: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Inverts exactly the window bit; post-window changed pairs refuse while in-window proceeds. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-admission: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Swallows exactly the landed drift refusal; every other admission refusal still surfaces. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-binding: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Drops exactly the evidence protocol arm; backend and implementation drift still refuse at this gate. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-identity: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Drops exactly the probe half of the substitution check; manifest and evidence aliases still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-kind: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the endpoint document as evidence; every other foreign kind still refuses, at the direct and emission entries. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resolve-manifest-count: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the four-ID double-manifest set; other ambiguous sets still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-status-prescan: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Skips the status pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4650,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1163,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
