{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000001090f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35d-fadf-7f82-925c-5ba6aefcf0a7"},"sequence":8930,"recorded_at":1780531400017855,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38ee7473-f77a-4937-9e67-866e0a213216"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3b1-93fd-7223-a9b9-afa9e7def864"},"task_id":"01a0b3b1-93fd-7223-a9b9-afa9e7def864","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3b1-93fd-7223-a9b9-afa9e7def864","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-263-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls .temp/TASK-260830-2056mm/cmd/ | head -40; echo ===; head -20 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check cmd logs and logbook\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"cmd01.log\\ncmd02.log\\ncmd03.log\\ncmd04.log\\ncmd05a.log\\ncmd05b.log\\ncmd05c.log\\ncmd05d.log\\ncmd05e.log\\ncmd05f.log\\ncmd05g.log\\ncmd05h.log\\ncmd06.log\\ncmd07.log\\ncmd08.log\\ncmd09.log\\ncmd10.log\\ncmd11.log\\ncmd12.log\\ncmd13.log\\ncmd14.log\\ncmd15.log\\ncmd16.log\\ncmd17.log\\ncmd18.log\\ncmd19.log\\ncmd20.log\\ncmd21.log\\ncmd22.log\\ncmd23.log\\ncmd24.log\\ncmd25.log\\ncmd26.log\\ncmd27.log\\ncmd28.log\\ncmd29.log\\ncmd30.log\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/termbind` — the §4.1/4.B-4.D/5.2-Terminal-Events/7.A final leaf over the landed owners and the story's own `axpane`/`terminstance`: `ParseTerminalBinding` owns the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object no parser existed for (ID recomputed before use, construction byte-agreed with the landed manifest admission); `CheckInstanceIdentity` + the operation-body pre-scans refuse the eight forbidden identity forms with the pinned protocol class on the Binding, descriptor (adopted landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts, with the CLI Result 4 surface a tripwire-pinned bound; `ResolveEvidence` resolves each v4 event's evidence IDs to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through the landed `Registry.AdmitProbe` (eleven foreign resolution targets refuse, substitution fails closed); `EmitTerminalCreated`/`EmitResumed` author the v4 payloads under a locally held lease with the digest as the opaque reference; `RecoverCreate` is read-only (absence / ONE child / unavailable+status_first, window from the fold newest); the attach receipt store records one durable receipt per client pair and emits neither event. Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, never a fork; v1 readers stay inert.\\n- F1: the producer's \\\"§13.1\\\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the pinned v0.7.0 document (\\\"status plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one child\\\") — §13.1's eight measured clauses are launch-plan/boot-direct/argv rules owned by another story, so the registry binds `section:4.1` (new, sliver 1/5) and leaves `section:13.1` untouched, with the mapping stated in the results.\\n- F2: a pre-scan gate is masked wherever the landed parser refuses with the identical code — the descriptor surface needed no wrapper (landed `AdmitProviderDescriptor` already pins `terminal_backend_protocol_error`), while the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals), and same-code reroutes (transport enum, evidence protocol arm, foreign-kind classification) need detail assertions or the mutant survives behind the landed twin.\\n- F3: the registry needed a reviewed-new-bindings extension — `assertNewBindingsAreReviewed` admitted only unevidenced stubs for sections the trunk baseline never bound, so `section:4.1` carries proof through a new `storyNewV070Bindings` list with literal matching plus clause remeasurement, mirroring the existing upgrade lists; seven new acceptance cases, four upgraded bindings (4.B/4.D/5.2 slivers, 7.A partial), digest re-pinned, tracecheck `63/574`.\\n- CLOSED the inherited residuals: axpane P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 (journal-only restore closure witness, the `EmitParked` winning-lease production binding with the mandated fix, corrupt-blob witness; the losing-lease test keeps its assertions with consistent-winner fixtures) and terminstance P3-1..P3-4 (five reviewer witnesses verbatim, three enum corpora extended, six mirrored rows); P3-2/P3-3 stated as owner bounds (pure-`Decide` unreachable shape; remote-owner closure-first failure, fail-closed).\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 28 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary arm-delete row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 30/30 with the harmless SURVIVED control), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits, production blobs byte-identical. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text. Extended batteries green: axpane 56/56 twice, terminstance 122/122.\\n- AC: 60 of 60 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via real SIGKILL on the attach and lost-create seams plus append-hook abort/replay. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev4 — Terminal Instance rework: grant-less fencing verdict, expiry recheck, P3 arms\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev3 (no P1; P2 F3 production, P2 E3 evidence, 5 P3; the reviewer confirmed F1/F2/E1/E2 closed, the harness 100/100 twice, the 84/84 ratio, and a green suite — all kept untouched): F3 lands the exported `fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner` verdict (direction/tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner, no grant precondition — a grant authorizes, it never decides staleness) and composes it in `ObserveFencing` for grant-gated refusals, so the no-grant, lapsed-grant, no-clock and unusable-policy members fence from active/parked/quiescing under local and remote winners while unverified/ambiguous/winnerless/malformed/handoff-failed stay no-transition with the gate's own refusal or park; E3 commits the auth-expiry recheck witness (mid-operation expiry caught after one committed effect) plus a harness row that keeps the tuple recheck and drops the expiry recheck, and re-keys both E1 expired members onto the late-deadline instant so they kill on the receipt; P3-1..P3-4 commit the four reviewer witnesses with mirror rows, and P3-5 states the interim-proven create member with its `unavailable → terminate-stale` exit route.\\n- F1: the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact for all four uniformly by never consulting grant/clock/policy, so completeness is structural, not enumerated, and the relative question needs no fallback (same grant facts, and the grant arms do not read `LocalHostID`).\\n- F2: a narrowing row that spans a definition and its use is one plant, not two — the E3 row captures the entry instant and passes it to the in-loop authorization check, and either half alone breaks the build, so the kill measures the pair (same precedent as the rev3 resumption row spanning two adjacent checks).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6545,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1637,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
